title: The attempt on the Shah
new-page: true

= 4 February 1949

An assailant wounds {!<span class="term term-royalist">!}Mohammad Reza
Shah{!</span>!} at Tehran University. The attack opens an immediate crisis:
claims about responsibility are uncertain, while coercive measures are already
being prepared.

- @attempt_caution: Insist publicly that evidence precede accusation
- @attempt_quiet: Gather reports before making a public intervention

@attempt_caution
on-arrival: constitutional_legitimacy += 2; prologue_legitimacy_modifier += 2
go-to: prologue_ban

You establish a constitutional standard without claiming knowledge the
opposition does not possess.

@attempt_quiet
on-arrival: political_intelligence += 2; prologue_intelligence_modifier += 2
go-to: prologue_ban

The network records conflicting reports and marks what remains unverified.

@prologue_ban
new-page: true

= Martial law and the Tudeh ban

Martial law follows the attack. The Tudeh Party is outlawed and opposition
press and political activity face new restrictions.

- @ban_legal_record: Build a legal record of emergency measures
- @ban_contacts: Preserve discreet organizational contacts

@ban_legal_record
on-arrival: constitutional_legitimacy += 2; prologue_legitimacy_modifier += 2; shah_relation -= 1; prologue_crown_modifier -= 1
go-to: prologue_constituent

@ban_contacts
on-arrival: organizational_reach += 2; prologue_organization_modifier += 2; political_intelligence += 1; prologue_intelligence_modifier += 1
go-to: prologue_constituent

@prologue_constituent
new-page: true

= The constituent assembly

The 1949 constituent assembly strengthens the Shah's constitutional position,
including a power to dissolve the Majles under revised Article 48.

- @assembly_procedure: Challenge the procedure and preserve a constitutional objection
- @assembly_risk: Concentrate on the practical risk of dissolution

@assembly_procedure
on-arrival: constitutional_legitimacy += 1; prologue_legitimacy_modifier += 1; shah_resistance += 2; prologue_crown_modifier -= 2
go-to: prologue_senate

@assembly_risk
on-arrival: political_intelligence += 2; prologue_intelligence_modifier += 2
go-to: prologue_senate

@prologue_senate
new-page: true

= A new Senate and a disputed election

Preparations for the first Senate coincide with the election for the Sixteenth
Majles. Opposition politicians must decide how to organize before scattered
complaints become a common campaign.

- @senate_committee: Prepare a common election-monitoring committee
- @senate_constitution: Prepare a public constitutional appeal

@senate_committee
on-arrival: organizational_reach += 1; prologue_organization_modifier += 1; prologue_complete = 1
go-to: palace_protest

@senate_constitution
on-arrival: public_mandate += 1; prologue_complete = 1
go-to: palace_protest
